        "agent_output": "All 776 tests pass.\n\n**The fix:** On line 457 of `blockprocessors.py`, the condition `self.TAG != 'ol'` was inverted. It should be `self.TAG == 'ol'` because integer start-value detection only applies to **ordered** lists (`ol`), not unordered lists (`ul`). The wrong condition caused the code to try matching an integer in unordered list items (which don't have numbers), resulting in the `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'group'`.\n"
