        "error": null,
        "agent_output": "All 776 tests pass, 110 skipped (pre-existing), 0 failures.\n\n**The bug:** In `markdown/blockprocessors.py` line 608, the `EmptyBlockProcessor` had an inverted condition:\n\n```python\nsibling[0].tag != 'code'  # Bug: should preserve blank lines IN code blocks\n```\n\nChanged to:\n\n```python\nsibling[0].tag == 'code'   # Fix: correctly identifies code blocks to preserve blank lines\n```\n\nThe `EmptyBlockProcessor` is responsible for preserving blank lines inside `<pre><code>` blocks. The condition was checking `!= 'code'` (meaning it would add blank line filler to everything *except* code blocks), when it should have been `== 'code'` (to add blank line filler specifically *to* code blocks). This caused consecutive blank lines inside indented code blocks to be collapsed instead of preserved.\n"
      }
    },
