        "error": null,
        "agent_output": "All 88 tests pass. \n\nThe bug was on line 246 of `markdown/core.py` in the `build_extension` method. The entry point filter used `!=` instead of `==`:\n\n```python\n# Bug: != causes it to match ALL other extensions, not the requested one\nep.name != ext_name\n\n# Fix: == correctly matches the requested extension name\nep.name == ext_name\n```\n\nThis inverted logic meant that when looking up an extension by name, the code would grab an unrelated entry point instead of the correct one (or fall through incorrectly), causing the `'markdown.extensions.footnotes:MissingExtension'` case to not raise the expected `AttributeError`.\n"
      }
